so um yeah interesting question and uh  something that we are pursuing with  bluemix thank you  wonderful and it looks like we've got  time for our last question  and we'll scooch back on over to dr  mayer  what are your plans for clinical  development of the p-car system  that's again a very interesting question  and  quite a few ideas really spring to mind  and  i guess the best validated target in  in car t at the moment is cd19  and i have shown you some data on the  panel of cd19p  cars that we have developed through  lucid and so we would be very interested  in evaluating a cd19  peak car in the clinic perhaps in in the  refractory  lymphoma setting so that's plan number  one i guess  and similarly in terms of the other mp  cars that i described  with potential application in the  context of solid tumors  i guess i'm particularly excited about  the nkg 2d  targeted parallel car systems and  given the the fact that these ligands  are a marker of stress  cells and of course tumor cells are a  form of stress cell  and the vast majority of both solid  tumors and hematological malignancies  express at least one of these nkg 2d  ligands  i think celiad as a company have done a  fantastic job  in developing the prototypic nkg2d  ligand  targeted car systems and they have  several clinical trials running in the  context of solid tumors  and hematological malignancies and to my  way of thinking  the the safety data that they have  generated to date is very encouraging  from the perspective of targeting nkg to  d ligands  so i would be very keen to evaluate  our mkg2d parallel car system in the  context of  uh refractory solid tumors which express  these ligands  thank you again dr reimers and dr mayor  do you have  any final comments for our audience  um no i think we had some very  interesting questions  uh and i would just like to thank  everybody for uh for joining our webinar  and have a good uh good day  and and could i just take the  opportunity to second that i'd like to  thank everybody for tuning in some  familiar and  participants and uh some um very  interesting questions  and i'd also like to express my thanks  to lumix for  for hosting this webinar  wonderful before we go i'd like to thank  the audience for joining us  joining us today and for their  interesting questions  questions we did not have time for today  and those submitted  during the on-demand period will be  addressed by the speakers via the  contact information that you provided at  the time of registration  we would like to once again thank dr  ramirez and dr  mayor for their time today and their  important research  we'd also like to thank leopards and our  sponsor lumix for underwriting today's  educational webcast  you can view the webinar on demand labs  will alert you via email when it's  available for replay  that's all for now stay healthy stay  safe  until next time bye
 

